timeline:
ONE uniform drives everything. JS each frame: const LOOP = 18.0; uPhaseT = (clock.getElapsedTime() % LOOP) / LOOP; At wrap (detect prevPhase > phase) advance shapeIndex = (shapeIndex+1)%3 and bind the next target texture to texTarget, and (re)set uBlastTime so the gaussian gate is fresh next cycle.

Phase windows on uPhaseT (18s loop -> seconds in parens):
  0.00-0.20 STREAM (0.0-3.6s): particles released from edges in hash-staggered waves; high uFlow curl, low uAttract, target = converge point vec3(0). Activation act = smoothstep(0, 0.5, mod(uTime - delay, LOOP)).
  0.20-0.235 SLAM/EXPLODE (3.6-4.23s): convergence pull peaks (ease-in pow(tConv,3)); the instant uPhaseT crosses 0.20 JS sets uBlastTime = uTime ONCE; velocity pass adds gaussian one-shot radial impulse pulse=exp(-age*age*60); uDamping drops 0.85->0.60; uAttract ~0.
  0.235-0.55 REFORM (4.23-9.9s): uExplode decays to 0, uAttract ramps 0.002->0.06 toward texTarget, curl turb fades 0.6->0.02; per-particle localProg = smoothstep(delay, delay+0.4, (uPhaseT-0.235)/0.315) gives the assembling wipe.
  0.55-0.82 HOLD/BREATHE (9.9-14.76s): uAttract high, curl ~0.03 shimmer, gl_PointSize *= 1.0+0.05*sin(uTime*1.4); shape sits still and alive.
  0.82-1.00 DISSOLVE (14.76-18.0s): uAttract->0, uFlow up, gentle outward bias + curl pushes particles to the edge-spawn shell (texOrigin); since dissolve target == next-loop spawn shell, the loop is SEAMLESS (no cut).

Derive all weights inside the sim shader with smoothstep windows (ease-in/out, no pops):
  float wStream   = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.18, 0.21, uPhaseT);
  float pulse     = smoothstep(0.200, 0.215, uPhaseT) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.215, 0.245, uPhaseT));
  float wReform   = smoothstep(0.235, 0.55, uPhaseT) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.80, 0.86, uPhaseT));
  float wDissolve = smoothstep(0.82, 1.00, uPhaseT);
  float uAttract  = mix(0.002, 0.06, wReform);
  float uFlow     = mix(0.35, 0.05, wReform) + wDissolve*0.40 + wStream*0.10;
  float uDamping  = mix(0.86, 0.60, pulse);
  float uExplode  = pulse * 6.0;
Important detail (MiniMax skill): use mod(uTime - delay, LOOP) for per-particle phase, NOT floor(uTime/LOOP)*LOOP (the latter adds a one-cycle startup dead time).

cameraAndViewport:
Single full-bleed canvas pinned behind the hero: CSS position:fixed/absolute inset:0; width:100vw; height:100vh; z-index:0; the H1/sub/CTA sit in a sibling layer z-index:10 with pointer-events passing through the canvas. The canvas element gets display:block so there is no inline-gap, and the renderer fills clientWidth x clientHeight.

Renderer/camera setup:
  renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias:false, alpha:true, powerPreference:'high-performance' });
  renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));  // HARD DPR clamp -- #1 cause of <60fps on a full-frame canvas
  renderer.setClearColor(0x05050f, 1);
  renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping; renderer.toneMappingExposure = 1.0;  // saturates the dense core instead of whiting out
  const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(55, aspect, 0.1, 100); camera.position.set(0,0,14);

Fit-to-viewport (the cure for the 'contained ball in the middle' failure): compute the world half-extents the camera actually sees at the particle plane z=0 and spawn/dissolve on a rectangle slightly LARGER than that frustum:
  const vFOV = camera.fov*Math.PI/180;
  const h = 2*Math.tan(vFOV/2)*Math.abs(camera.position.z);  // visible height at z=0
  const w = h*camera.aspect;                                  // visible width at z=0
  uFrustum.value.set(w, h);  // fed to sim + render so dissolve targets scale with the frame
Spawn shell half-extents = frustum*0.625 then pushed out *1.15 so streaks ENTER from beyond the edge (point sprites are culled by center, so spawning just past +/-1 avoids edge-pop). Spread target z across [-camZ*0.6, +camZ*0.4] so the frame reads volumetric (near/far size-attenuation glow gradient), not a flat sheet. Recompute w/h/uFrustum and renderer size on every resize (ResizeObserver on the container). Keep PerspectiveCamera (NOT ortho) so gl_PointSize = uSize*uDpr / -mvPosition.z gives the depth glow gradient. Coverage comes from frustum math, never from zoom.

positionShader:
// === simPosition.frag (GPUComputationRenderer; 'resolution' + texturePosition/textureVelocity auto-injected) ===
uniform float uDt;
void main() {
  vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / resolution.xy;
  vec4 posTex = texture2D(texturePosition, uv);
  vec3 pos = posTex.xyz;
  float seed = posTex.a;            // preserve per-particle seed across frames
  vec3 vel = texture2D(textureVelocity, uv).xyz;
  // Symplectic Euler: velocity pass already integrated forces this step.
  pos += vel * uDt;
  gl_FragColor = vec4(pos, seed);   // carry seed forward untouched
}

Notes: uDt is the clamped frame delta (clamp to <=1/30 so a tab-stall never explodes the sim). No target logic lives here -- position is pure integration; all forces are in the velocity pass so damping/impulse/spring stay in one place (the Codrops Dec-2024 two-pass split).

velocityShader:
// === simVelocity.frag (GPUComputationRenderer) ===
// Auto-injected by GPUComputationRenderer: texturePosition, textureVelocity, resolution.
uniform float uTime, uPhaseT, uDt, uBlastTime;
uniform vec2  uFrustum;
uniform sampler2D texOrigin;   // edge-spawn shell (STREAM src / DISSOLVE dst)
uniform sampler2D texTarget;   // current shape slot (brain/constellation/lattice)
#define PI 3.14159265

// ---- simplex noise snoise(vec3) : paste Ashima/webgl-noise 3D simplex here (standard 80-line impl) ----
vec3 snoiseVec3(vec3 p){ return vec3( snoise(p),
                                      snoise(p+vec3(17.1, 9.2, 3.3)),
                                      snoise(p+vec3(101.7,5.4,71.2)) ); }
vec3 curlNoise(vec3 p){            // cabbibo/glsl-curl-noise, divergence-free
  const float e=0.1; vec3 dx=vec3(e,0,0),dy=vec3(0,e,0),dz=vec3(0,0,e);
  vec3 px0=snoiseVec3(p-dx),px1=snoiseVec3(p+dx);
  vec3 py0=snoiseVec3(p-dy),py1=snoiseVec3(p+dy);
  vec3 pz0=snoiseVec3(p-dz),pz1=snoiseVec3(p+dz);
  float x=py1.z-py0.z-pz1.y+pz0.y;
  float y=pz1.x-pz0.x-px1.z+px0.z;
  float z=px1.y-px0.y-py1.x+py0.x;
  return normalize(vec3(x,y,z)/(2.0*e));
}
float hash11(float p){ return fract(sin(p*127.1)*43758.5453); }

void main(){
  vec2 uv  = gl_FragCoord.xy / resolution.xy;
  vec4 pT  = texture2D(texturePosition, uv);
  vec3 pos = pT.xyz; float seed = pT.a;
  vec3 vel = texture2D(textureVelocity, uv).xyz;
  vec3 originPos = texture2D(texOrigin, uv).xyz;
  float perimT   = texture2D(texOrigin, uv).a;
  vec4 tgtTex    = texture2D(texTarget, uv);
  vec3 shapePos  = tgtTex.xyz;

  // ---- per-phase weights (smoothstep windows, no pops) ----
  float wStream   = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.18, 0.21, uPhaseT);
  float pulse     = smoothstep(0.200, 0.215, uPhaseT) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.215, 0.245, uPhaseT));
  float wReform   = smoothstep(0.235, 0.55, uPhaseT) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.80, 0.86, uPhaseT));
  float wDissolve = smoothstep(0.82, 1.00, uPhaseT);

  // ---- STREAM: hash-staggered release toward center, curl tendrils ----
  float delay = 0.10*hash11(seed*91.7) + 0.08*perimT;      // random + clockwise sweep
  float act   = smoothstep(0.0, 0.06, uPhaseT - delay);    // 0 until this particle's turn
  vec3 toCenter = -pos;                                     // center = vec3(0)
  float dC = length(toCenter);
  vec3 dirC = toCenter / max(dC, 1e-4);
  // ease-in convergence: slow drift -> violent collapse as we approach the slam (uPhaseT->0.20)
  float tConv = clamp(uPhaseT/0.20, 0.0, 1.0);
  float pull  = pow(tConv, 3.0);
  vel += dirC * (0.01 + 0.12*pull) * act * wStream * smoothstep(0.0, 6.0, dC);

  // ---- EXPLODE: one-shot gaussian radial blast (the SLAM), core launches hardest ----
  float age   = uTime - uBlastTime;
  float gate  = exp(-age*age*60.0);                        // ~1 frame wide -> reads as impact not push
  vec3  fromC = pos;
  float r     = max(length(fromC), 1e-4);
  vec3  outDir= fromC / r;
  float falloff = 1.0/(1.0 + r*r*4.0);                     // inverse-square-ish
  vel += outDir * 6.0 * falloff * gate;
  vel += (snoiseVec3(pos*31.0)) * 0.06 * gate;             // jitter so the front is not a perfect sphere

  // ---- REFORM/HOLD: spring onto shape target with staggered per-particle wipe ----
  float localProg = smoothstep(delay, delay+0.40, (uPhaseT-0.235)/0.315); // assembling sweep
  float kAttract  = mix(0.002, 0.06, wReform) * localProg;
  vec3 toShape = shapePos - pos; float dS = length(toShape);
  vel += (toShape / max(dS,1e-4)) * kAttract * dS;         // Hookean: stronger when far

  // ---- DISSOLVE: fade spring, ramp curl + outward bias toward the edge shell ----
  vec3 toEdge = originPos - pos;
  vel += toEdge * (0.01 * wDissolve);                      // gently retarget to next-loop spawn
  vel += normalize(pos + 1e-4) * 0.004 * wDissolve;        // outward bias fills viewport

  // ---- curl turbulence: strong on stream/explode, ~0 once formed (keeps brain crisp) ----
  float turb = (0.35*wStream + 0.18*gate + 0.40*wDissolve) + mix(0.04, 0.015, wReform);
  vel += curlNoise(pos*0.30 + uTime*0.10) * turb * uDt * 12.0;

  // ---- damping + velocity cap (stable slam) ----
  float damping = mix(0.86, 0.60, pulse);
  vel *= damping;
  float vmax = 3.0; float v = length(vel); if (v > vmax) vel *= vmax / v;

  gl_FragColor = vec4(vel, 1.0);
}

renderShader:
// ===================== render VERTEX shader =====================
uniform sampler2D texturePosition;
uniform sampler2D textureVelocity;
uniform float uSize, uDpr, uPhaseT, uTime;
attribute vec2 reference;        // uv into the sim textures (baked per vertex)
varying float vSpeed;
varying float vRole;             // node(1) vs edge(0) from target.a -- but we pass seed-based hue too
varying float vSeed;
varying vec3  vWorld;
void main(){
  vec4 posTex = texture2D(texturePosition, reference);
  vec3 pos    = posTex.xyz; vSeed = posTex.a;
  vec3 vel    = texture2D(textureVelocity, reference).xyz;
  vSpeed = length(vel);
  vWorld = pos;
  vec4 mv = modelViewMatrix * vec4(pos, 1.0);
  // breathe during HOLD (0.55-0.82) only
  float breathe = 1.0 + 0.05*sin(uTime*1.4) * step(0.55,uPhaseT) * step(uPhaseT,0.82);
  // velocity-stretch: fast edge streamers get bigger (comet feel); settled dots stay small
  float stretch = 1.0 + clamp(vSpeed*0.6, 0.0, 2.5);
  gl_PointSize = uSize * uDpr * breathe * stretch / max(-mv.z, 0.1);
  gl_Position = projectionMatrix * mv;
}

// ===================== render FRAGMENT shader =====================
precision highp float;
uniform vec3 uViolet;   // 0.39,0.40,0.95  (0x6366f1)
uniform vec3 uCyan;     // 0.13,0.83,0.93  (0x22d3ee)
uniform vec3 uEmerald;  // 0.20,0.83,0.60  (0x34d399)
uniform vec2 uTextCenterNDC;  // headline center in [0,1] screen uv (~0.5,0.5)
uniform vec2 uResolution;
varying float vSpeed; varying float vSeed; varying vec3 vWorld;
void main(){
  // soft round sprite -- NO hard disc, so additive overlap accumulates as glow not a white plate
  vec2 q = gl_PointCoord - 0.5;
  float d = length(q);
  float a = exp(-d*d*5.0);                      // gaussian falloff sprite
  if (a < 0.01) discard;
  // palette: split hue by seed so violet/cyan/emerald separate SPATIALLY (never average to white)
  vec3 col = mix(uViolet, uCyan, smoothstep(0.0,0.5,vSeed));
  col = mix(col, uEmerald, smoothstep(0.5,1.0,vSeed));
  // fast particles flash slightly hotter (toward cyan) so the slam reads energetic
  col = mix(col, uCyan, clamp(vSpeed*0.12, 0.0, 0.5));
  // LOW base so N-overlap stays in-gamut and HUED (this is the anti-white-out lever)
  col *= 0.38;
  // dim behind the headline bounding box so text stays legible even at the explosion peak
  vec2 sUv = gl_FragCoord.xy / uResolution;
  float textMask = smoothstep(0.0, 0.22, length(sUv - uTextCenterNDC));
  float alpha = a * (0.55 + 0.45*textMask);
  gl_FragColor = vec4(col * alpha, alpha);     // AdditiveBlending, depthWrite:false
}

Material: new THREE.ShaderMaterial({ blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending, depthWrite:false, depthTest:false, transparent:true, uniforms:{...} }). Render to the composer; UnrealBloom strength 0.7, radius 0.45, THRESHOLD 0.55 -- the 0.38 base sits BELOW threshold so only hot cores/the slam bloom, keeping the center violet/cyan not a white disc. ACESFilmic tone mapping on the renderer finishes the anti-clip.

targetShapes:
Build THREE target DataTextures once at boot, all in the SAME texel order the particles read (texel i -> particle i), all RGBA FloatType, NearestFilter, ClampToEdge. Channel a = role (1=node bright/large, 0=edge/fill dim/small).

SHAPE A -- BRAIN (organic, mesh-sampled): load a low-poly brain GLB (Draco) OR fall back to two merged icospheres squashed into hemispheres. Use three/addons/math/MeshSurfaceSampler:
  import { MeshSurfaceSampler } from 'three/addons/math/MeshSurfaceSampler.js';
  const sampler = new MeshSurfaceSampler(brainMesh).build();
  const p=new THREE.Vector3(), n=new THREE.Vector3();
  for(let i=0;i<N;i++){ sampler.sample(p,n); p.addScaledVector(n, -Math.random()*0.15); // push inward => volumetric fill
    data[i*4]=p.x*S; data[i*4+1]=p.y*S; data[i*4+2]=p.z*S; data[i*4+3]= Math.random()<0.5?1.0:0.0; }
  Scale S so the brain spans ~70% of uFrustum height.

SHAPE B -- MEMORY-GRAPH CONSTELLATION (no mesh): Fibonacci-sphere nodes + edge particles painting connections.
  const GA=Math.PI*(3.0-Math.sqrt(5.0)); const M=600; // node count
  for(let k=0;k<M;k++){ const y=1-(k/(M-1))*2, r=Math.sqrt(1-y*y), t=GA*k; nodes[k]=new THREE.Vector3(Math.cos(t)*r,y,Math.sin(t)*r).multiplyScalar(R); }
  // precompute edges: connect a->b if dist<edgeRadius. Then assign particles:
  //   ~35% NODE particles: target = nodes[k] (+ small jitter), role=1
  //   ~65% EDGE particles: target = mix(nodes[a], nodes[b], seed) along a chosen edge, role=0
  This turns a point cloud into a READABLE network (nodes bright, filaments faint).

SHAPE C -- NEURAL LATTICE (crystalline): hash-jittered 3D grid.
  cell = floor(gridIndex); center = (cell+0.5)*cellSize - half; jitter = (hash3(cell)-0.5)*0.55*cellSize;
  target = center + jitter; role: particles near a grid LINE (one axis ~integer) = node(1), interior = fill(0).
  Edge particles lerp along lattice struts (mix of two adjacent cell centers by seed) for visible connectivity.

SWITCHING: keep targetTextures = [brainTex, constellationTex, latticeTex]. On loop wrap (prevPhase>phase) set velocityVar.material.uniforms.texTarget.value = targetTextures[++shapeIndex % 3] and renderMaterial likewise if it samples target. Because every particle keeps its texel index, the morph from edge-shell -> shape is clean point-to-point; no re-sort needed. (Loopspeed FBO multi-target mix pattern.)
